After playing for 18 years, and three years since my YAFAP I have finally 
done it, this healer means I have ascended every class at least once!

I played healers exclusively since ascending my caveman back in march, 
killing many in many stupid ways.  There weren't any post worthy YASD's in 
there, but many, many deaths.  As is usually the case, (for me at least) a 
WoW (on the oracle level) was the turning point.  I had given up on the 
protection racket, the first level of the mines was unlit and had two 
hostile dwarves in sight.  I had found a key on level 3 and  decided to head 
for sokoban.  Being level 4 and having ~30 hps when the engrave test came 
out the best possible way I burned the first wish on the PYEC.  (MR for 
polyselfless, free Telepathy, and limited free charging)  I then wished for 
a SDSM and Speed boots (wand was 0:3, I would have been ticked off if I got 
a luck wrest on a 0:1 or 0:2 wand but I took the chance.)  I then waited to 
heal up and invoked the PYEC to recharge.  I then got a HoB and 2 markers 
for later.  Sokoban had the bag and my cat Puss Puss killed a white unicorn 
for me so I had my pre-quest weapon.  I managed to poke my way down to 
minetown, making basic in unihorn along the way, the temple was cross 
aligned.  I price id'ed identify, BUC showed it was blessed and had the luck 
to get a full ID on the first try, so I knew EW and EA in minetown.  The 
general store also had a [oDisplacement.  I headed back to the oracle level 
to rinse out some un-needed scrolls (DA, Punish and a few ?oLight) I 
scribbled enough EA and EW to get an ac of around -13 and a +5 Unihorn. 
Back to the mines, picking up a magic whistle one level below minetown, 
taming a couple of pets with meatballs i'm becoming a bit of a force. 
Minesend (mimic of the mines) yeilds the luckstone and a polytrap.  Here 
Puss Puss.  I leave minesend with a Balrog, a Couatl and a yellow dragon. 
The guard/merchants of minetown don't stand a chance... I do lock away the 
keeper of the lights (bad karma to allow him to die)  The priest accepts all 
the found gold and provides 5 points of ac, then I whistle in the refund 
team and reclaim my gold plus a robe and spellbooks.

Heading back to the main dungeon I use the shopkeepers /oStriking to break 
open the oracle level statues, netting +oMagic Mapping and RC.  While i'm 
reading books, Puss kills the oracle and the dragon eats the corpse.  Oh, 
well, the gold will go elsewhere.  I peeked through the quest portal, not 
having any way to cross to the main island and seeing a black dragon on one 
of the islands, I backed out and headed down.  No Bigroom, No ludoius, Rogue 
level had one bones pile, no fAoY.

On level 22 or so back to back tengu gave me TC and Teleportitis,  this 
would help out later in the game.

Medusa was the right island one with the titan, he threw a boulder at me on 
my second move, so I waited behind it for Puss and co to kill it.  They did 
so and I then gathered them at the uppper end of the room and dug down.  One 
maze level, found the upstairs first and stoned Medusa, then went down and 
used the boulder corridor and /oStriking method of entering.  After a brisk 
fight I get my second /oW.  The castle armory is guarded by 4 Yellow 
dragons, but yeilds [Lev and WW so I fill out my AK with [GoD and a Hawiian 
shirt.  I used the WW boots to rinse off enough scrolls to finish enchanting 
my gear, AC -35 and a +7 unihorn at expert allow me to play as a combat 
wombat with my pets for backup.  I clear the VotD and get 4 more points of 
protection from the priest of moloch.  Time for the quest.

The quest levels were easy, until the cyclops showed.  He got a level off me 
before I used my starting /oSleep to sedate him for the evisceration.  He 
never regained consciousness.  I levitated over onto his island and among 
the junk was yet another WoW.  No lack of wishes this game.

I enchanted up the Staff and used it on anything that wasn't level drain 
resistant, switching to the unihorn for nasties that were.

Ghennom is better left forgotten, Baalz was a bonesfile with the statue of 
my lizard corpseless Caveman.  I broke it down, trading my Displacement for 
his Oilskin and my SDSM for his GDSM.  Orcus refused to give up his stick 
before wasting a couple of charges on me and killing my non-demonic pets. 
Puss ended up steping on a levelporter shortly after so I did the late game 
petless (no +oCharm and I didn't wish for one)  Rodney didn't like the look 
of Orcus' wand and left me his book in the will.

The sanctum was annoying due to a master lich who refused to be unihorned to 
death.  It did eventually go down, after I got the amulet and walked back to 
the stairs.

On teleport levels I rarely stayed more than a dozen turns, teleportits 
would kick in and away I go.  The force wasn't too hard on me, 5 push backs 
and none back to Juby's swamp.

The planes were a mixed bag.  On earth and fire the portal was close, on air 
and water it was as far a possible.  Air elementals weren't a big problem 
with the Staff draining them and healing me, a titan made fire tricky, but a 
rubber chicken put a stop to the summoning storm.  Water was just a bore 
with the bubble seemingly taking forever to reach the portal.

Astral required the full tour, although I did manage to dodge Death and 
Pesty on death's branch (the right one), buffering myself with tamed 
insects.  An under equipped player monster (a Knight) was in the high 
temple, I killed him and dragged his gear to the altar, strange set of gear.
